{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"differenceY"},{"type":"text","value":" compares two numeric y channels along a numeric or temporal x\nchannel. It fills positive and negative lobes and draws both boundary lines.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"differenceX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes the same semantics to two numeric x channels along a\nnumeric or temporal y channel."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { differenceY } from '@tanstack/charts/difference'\n\ndifferenceY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y1: 'forecast',\n  y2: 'actual',\n  positiveFill: '#16a34a',\n  negativeFill: '#dc2626',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function differenceY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction differenceX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"differenceY"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":" is the comparison and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2"},{"type":"text","value":" is the primary value. A\npositive lobe means "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2 > y1"},{"type":"text","value":"; a negative lobe means "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2 < y1"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"differenceX"},{"type":"text","value":" applies the same rule to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":" values. One\nmark input cannot mix the two kinds. The value channels accept numeric\nconstants or channels. Input order is path order; sort rows before creating the\nmark when the semantic independent order differs from source order. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" to\ncompare one pair of lines per first-seen group."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"crossing-and-gap-semantics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Crossing and gap semantics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At every sign change, the mark maps both boundary segments through the final\nx and y scales, solves their exact rendered crossing, and inverts that point\nback to semantic values. The result remains exact with nonlinear log, power,\nor symlog scales instead of assuming data-space interpolation is affine. Both\nconfigured positional scales must support inversion."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The crossing belongs to both adjacent lobes, so the fills meet without overlap\nor a gap. Consecutive equal values remain part of the neighboring lobe instead\nof producing one-point areas."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A row with an invalid independent, comparison, or primary value creates the\nsame gap in both areas and both lines. Later valid rows begin new segments.\nThe mark composes ordinary "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaY"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineY"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineX"},{"type":"text","value":" children; it does\nnot emit a case-specific path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable composite mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orientation-specific "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric or temporal independent value"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison boundary"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary boundary"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Independent comparison groups"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable raw-row and derived-lobe identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"positiveFill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#3ca951"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Positive-lobe paint; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" omits the fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"negativeFill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#4269d0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Negative-lobe paint; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" omits the fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared fill opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"positiveFillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Positive-lobe opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"negativeFillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Negative-lobe opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary-line paint"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary-line opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2.25"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary-line width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary-line dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"comparisonStroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#64748b"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison-line paint"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"comparisonStrokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison-line opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"comparisonStrokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison-line width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"comparisonStrokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison-line dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Draws points on both boundary lines"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary-line focus presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"comparisonStates"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison-line focus presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition<DifferenceDatum<...>>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion over raw boundaries and derived area rows"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The orientation determines the exact channel types. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DifferenceYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"\nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DifferenceXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" when naming an options object separately. The two fill\nchannels receive derived area rows; the line paint and state channels receive\nthe original source rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived data and lineage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Area children receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DifferenceAreaDatum"},{"type":"text","value":" rows:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> {\n  kind: 'difference-area'\n  independent: TIndependent\n  comparison: number\n  primary: number\n  sign: 'positive' | 'negative'\n  segment: string\n  crossing: boolean\n  markKey: ChartKey\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}\n\ntype DifferenceDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> =\n  TDatum | DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public type surface also includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DifferenceIndependent"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DifferenceSign"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An original area point retains its source row and index. An interpolated\ncrossing retains both adjacent source rows and indexes. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"segment"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markKey"},{"type":"text","value":" derive from stable group and source-boundary identity, so prepending\nan unrelated lobe does not rename later geometry."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The positive and negative areas are decorative. The comparison and primary\nlines each contribute interaction points that retain the original source-row\nidentity. Their child mark IDs end in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":comparison"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":primary"},{"type":"text","value":", allowing a\ntooltip or selection handler to distinguish the two values without receiving\nsynthetic crossing rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set either fill to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" to render one-sided emphasis. Set both to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" to\nretain the two interactive boundary lines without areas."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"signatures","text":"Signatures","level":2},{"id":"crossing-and-gap-semantics","text":"Crossing and gap semantics","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","text":"Derived data and lineage","level":2},{"id":"interaction","text":"Interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`differenceY` compares two numeric y channels along a numeric or temporal x\nchannel. It fills positive and negative lobes and draws both boundary lines.\n`differenceX` transposes the same semantics to two numeric x channels along a\nnumeric or temporal y channel.\n\n```ts\nimport { differenceY } from '@tanstack/charts/difference'\n\ndifferenceY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y1: 'forecast',\n  y2: 'actual',\n  positiveFill: '#16a34a',\n  negativeFill: '#dc2626',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction differenceY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction differenceX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n```\n\nFor `differenceY`, `y1` is the comparison and `y2` is the primary value. A\npositive lobe means `y2 > y1`; a negative lobe means `y2 < y1`.\n`differenceX` applies the same rule to `x1` and `x2`.\n\nThe independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid `Date` values. One\nmark input cannot mix the two kinds. The value channels accept numeric\nconstants or channels. Input order is path order; sort rows before creating the\nmark when the semantic independent order differs from source order. Set `z` to\ncompare one pair of lines per first-seen group.\n\n## Crossing and gap semantics\n\nAt every sign change, the mark maps both boundary segments through the final\nx and y scales, solves their exact rendered crossing, and inverts that point\nback to semantic values. The result remains exact with nonlinear log, power,\nor symlog scales instead of assuming data-space interpolation is affine. Both\nconfigured positional scales must support inversion.\n\nThe crossing belongs to both adjacent lobes, so the fills meet without overlap\nor a gap. Consecutive equal values remain part of the neighboring lobe instead\nof producing one-point areas.\n\nA row with an invalid independent, comparison, or primary value creates the\nsame gap in both areas and both lines. Later valid rows begin new segments.\nThe mark composes ordinary `areaY`/`areaX` and `lineY`/`lineX` children; it does\nnot emit a case-specific path.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                      | Type                                                 | Default         | Meaning                                          |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `id`                        | `string`                                             | Layer-derived   | Stable composite mark ID                         |\n| `x` / `y`                   | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required        | Numeric or temporal independent value            |\n| `y1` / `x1`                 | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required        | Comparison boundary                              |\n| `y2` / `x2`                 | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required        | Primary boundary                                 |\n| `z`                         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                         | One group       | Independent comparison groups                    |\n| `key`                       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                          | Inferred        | Stable raw-row and derived-lobe identity         |\n| `positiveFill`              | `VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> \\| null` | `#3ca951`       | Positive-lobe paint; `null` omits the fill       |\n| `negativeFill`              | `VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> \\| null` | `#4269d0`       | Negative-lobe paint; `null` omits the fill       |\n| `fillOpacity`               | `number`                                             | `0.2`           | Shared fill opacity                              |\n| `positiveFillOpacity`       | `number`                                             | `fillOpacity`   | Positive-lobe opacity                            |\n| `negativeFillOpacity`       | `number`                                             | `fillOpacity`   | Negative-lobe opacity                            |\n| `stroke`                    | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`                      | `currentColor`  | Primary-line paint                               |\n| `strokeOpacity`             | `number`                                             | SVG default     | Primary-line opacity                             |\n| `strokeWidth`               | `number`                                             | `2.25`          | Primary-line width                               |\n| `strokeDasharray`           | `string`                                             | None            | Primary-line dash pattern                        |\n| `comparisonStroke`          | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`                      | `#64748b`       | Comparison-line paint                            |\n| `comparisonStrokeOpacity`   | `number`                                             | `strokeOpacity` | Comparison-line opacity                          |\n| `comparisonStrokeWidth`     | `number`                                             | `strokeWidth`   | Comparison-line width                            |\n| `comparisonStrokeDasharray` | `string`                                             | None            | Comparison-line dash pattern                     |\n| `points`                    | `boolean`                                            | `false`         | Draws points on both boundary lines              |\n| `states`                    | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                          | None            | Primary-line focus presentation                  |\n| `comparisonStates`          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                          | None            | Comparison-line focus presentation               |\n| `motion`                    | `ChartMotionDefinition<DifferenceDatum<...>>`        | None            | Motion over raw boundaries and derived area rows |\n\nThe orientation determines the exact channel types. Use `DifferenceYOptions`\nor `DifferenceXOptions` when naming an options object separately. The two fill\nchannels receive derived area rows; the line paint and state channels receive\nthe original source rows.\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nArea children receive `DifferenceAreaDatum` rows:\n\n```ts\ninterface DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> {\n  kind: 'difference-area'\n  independent: TIndependent\n  comparison: number\n  primary: number\n  sign: 'positive' | 'negative'\n  segment: string\n  crossing: boolean\n  markKey: ChartKey\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}\n\ntype DifferenceDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> =\n  TDatum | DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent>\n```\n\nThe public type surface also includes `DifferenceIndependent` and\n`DifferenceSign`.\n\nAn original area point retains its source row and index. An interpolated\ncrossing retains both adjacent source rows and indexes. `segment` and\n`markKey` derive from stable group and source-boundary identity, so prepending\nan unrelated lobe does not rename later geometry.\n\n## Interaction\n\nThe positive and negative areas are decorative. The comparison and primary\nlines each contribute interaction points that retain the original source-row\nidentity. Their child mark IDs end in `:comparison` and `:primary`, allowing a\ntooltip or selection handler to distinguish the two values without receiving\nsynthetic crossing rows.\n\nSet either fill to `null` to render one-sided emphasis. Set both to `null` to\nretain the two interactive boundary lines without areas.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Difference Marks\ndescription: Reference for differenceY and differenceX comparison areas, exact crossings, grouping, gaps, lineage, styling, and interaction.\n---\n\n`differenceY` compares two numeric y channels along a numeric or temporal x\nchannel. It fills positive and negative lobes and draws both boundary lines.\n`differenceX` transposes the same semantics to two numeric x channels along a\nnumeric or temporal y channel.\n\n```ts\nimport { differenceY } from '@tanstack/charts/difference'\n\ndifferenceY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y1: 'forecast',\n  y2: 'actual',\n  positiveFill: '#16a34a',\n  negativeFill: '#dc2626',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction differenceY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction differenceX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: DifferenceXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<DifferenceDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n```\n\nFor `differenceY`, `y1` is the comparison and `y2` is the primary value. A\npositive lobe means `y2 > y1`; a negative lobe means `y2 < y1`.\n`differenceX` applies the same rule to `x1` and `x2`.\n\nThe independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid `Date` values. One\nmark input cannot mix the two kinds. The value channels accept numeric\nconstants or channels. Input order is path order; sort rows before creating the\nmark when the semantic independent order differs from source order. Set `z` to\ncompare one pair of lines per first-seen group.\n\n## Crossing and gap semantics\n\nAt every sign change, the mark maps both boundary segments through the final\nx and y scales, solves their exact rendered crossing, and inverts that point\nback to semantic values. The result remains exact with nonlinear log, power,\nor symlog scales instead of assuming data-space interpolation is affine. Both\nconfigured positional scales must support inversion.\n\nThe crossing belongs to both adjacent lobes, so the fills meet without overlap\nor a gap. Consecutive equal values remain part of the neighboring lobe instead\nof producing one-point areas.\n\nA row with an invalid independent, comparison, or primary value creates the\nsame gap in both areas and both lines. Later valid rows begin new segments.\nThe mark composes ordinary `areaY`/`areaX` and `lineY`/`lineX` children; it does\nnot emit a case-specific path.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                      | Type                                                 | Default         | Meaning                                          |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `id`                        | `string`                                             | Layer-derived   | Stable composite mark ID                         |\n| `x` / `y`                   | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required        | Numeric or temporal independent value            |\n| `y1` / `x1`                 | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required        | Comparison boundary                              |\n| `y2` / `x2`                 | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required        | Primary boundary                                 |\n| `z`                         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                         | One group       | Independent comparison groups                    |\n| `key`                       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                          | Inferred        | Stable raw-row and derived-lobe identity         |\n| `positiveFill`              | `VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> \\| null` | `#3ca951`       | Positive-lobe paint; `null` omits the fill       |\n| `negativeFill`              | `VisualChannel<DifferenceAreaDatum, string> \\| null` | `#4269d0`       | Negative-lobe paint; `null` omits the fill       |\n| `fillOpacity`               | `number`                                             | `0.2`           | Shared fill opacity                              |\n| `positiveFillOpacity`       | `number`                                             | `fillOpacity`   | Positive-lobe opacity                            |\n| `negativeFillOpacity`       | `number`                                             | `fillOpacity`   | Negative-lobe opacity                            |\n| `stroke`                    | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`                      | `currentColor`  | Primary-line paint                               |\n| `strokeOpacity`             | `number`                                             | SVG default     | Primary-line opacity                             |\n| `strokeWidth`               | `number`                                             | `2.25`          | Primary-line width                               |\n| `strokeDasharray`           | `string`                                             | None            | Primary-line dash pattern                        |\n| `comparisonStroke`          | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`                      | `#64748b`       | Comparison-line paint                            |\n| `comparisonStrokeOpacity`   | `number`                                             | `strokeOpacity` | Comparison-line opacity                          |\n| `comparisonStrokeWidth`     | `number`                                             | `strokeWidth`   | Comparison-line width                            |\n| `comparisonStrokeDasharray` | `string`                                             | None            | Comparison-line dash pattern                     |\n| `points`                    | `boolean`                                            | `false`         | Draws points on both boundary lines              |\n| `states`                    | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                          | None            | Primary-line focus presentation                  |\n| `comparisonStates`          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                          | None            | Comparison-line focus presentation               |\n| `motion`                    | `ChartMotionDefinition<DifferenceDatum<...>>`        | None            | Motion over raw boundaries and derived area rows |\n\nThe orientation determines the exact channel types. Use `DifferenceYOptions`\nor `DifferenceXOptions` when naming an options object separately. The two fill\nchannels receive derived area rows; the line paint and state channels receive\nthe original source rows.\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nArea children receive `DifferenceAreaDatum` rows:\n\n```ts\ninterface DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> {\n  kind: 'difference-area'\n  independent: TIndependent\n  comparison: number\n  primary: number\n  sign: 'positive' | 'negative'\n  segment: string\n  crossing: boolean\n  markKey: ChartKey\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}\n\ntype DifferenceDatum<TDatum, TIndependent> =\n  TDatum | DifferenceAreaDatum<TDatum, TIndependent>\n```\n\nThe public type surface also includes `DifferenceIndependent` and\n`DifferenceSign`.\n\nAn original area point retains its source row and index. An interpolated\ncrossing retains both adjacent source rows and indexes. `segment` and\n`markKey` derive from stable group and source-boundary identity, so prepending\nan unrelated lobe does not rename later geometry.\n\n## Interaction\n\nThe positive and negative areas are decorative. The comparison and primary\nlines each contribute interaction points that retain the original source-row\nidentity. Their child mark IDs end in `:comparison` and `:primary`, allowing a\ntooltip or selection handler to distinguish the two values without receiving\nsynthetic crossing rows.\n\nSet either fill to `null` to render one-sided emphasis. Set both to `null` to\nretain the two interactive boundary lines without areas.\n"}
